What's going to happen to the market?

235
00:16:07,052 --> 00:16:11,552
It can drop. Say they're buying when they're no longer there to support the market.

236
00:16:11,552 --> 00:16:13,252
What's going to happen? The market's going to fall.

237
00:16:14,052 --> 00:16:20,452
That's why it's important to notice when institutional traders are active and when they're not active in the market.

238
00:16:21,952 --> 00:16:23,252
There's no secret to trading.

239
00:16:25,052 --> 00:16:27,540
Successful trading has always been about understanding the

240
00:16:27,540 --> 00:16:30,028
convictions, the strengths, the weaknesses of buyers and

241
00:16:30,028 --> 00:16:33,450
sellers, especially the ones with the money to move the markets.

242
00:16:34,652 --> 00:16:38,952
You don't necessarily care about what all the little retail traders are doing.

243
00:16:40,352 --> 00:16:44,452
Granted, you can add them all up and get a big collective, but

244
00:16:45,252 --> 00:16:49,852
You know, retail traders, they're trading for many different reasons.

245
00:16:49,852 --> 00:16:54,352
You know, they've got indicators, they've got trading advice from somebody.

246
00:16:55,552 --> 00:16:58,752
You know, the people with the big money, they have the conviction of the market.

247
00:16:59,052 --> 00:17:02,052
You know, a retail trader doesn't necessarily have the conviction of the market.

248
00:17:02,152 --> 00:17:04,852
And an institutional big trader, you know,

249
00:17:05,552 --> 00:17:12,552
They can withstand the market, take a little heat from the market as it moves against them, a retail trader.

250
00:17:12,952 --> 00:17:18,952
As soon as it starts turning against them by a couple points, they start to panic and get out.

251
00:17:20,252 --> 00:17:24,752
Institutional traders, they can assess the market and decide, do they still want to be in?

252
00:17:25,552 --> 00:17:26,956
And most often, if they

253
00:17:26,956 --> 00:17:28,922
still want to be in, they may

254
00:17:28,922 --> 00:17:31,450
be interested in building up their position even more.

255
00:17:31,852 --> 00:17:36,852
So once you understand what the institutional traders are doing in the market, You can trade with them.

256
00:17:37,252 --> 00:17:41,152
You want to be trading with the traders who are moving the prices.

257
00:17:41,752 --> 00:17:43,952
You don't want to be trading against them.

258
00:17:45,052 --> 00:17:48,252
You want to be on the right side as them.

259
00:17:48,752 --> 00:17:50,152
Think of it like...

260
00:17:51,752 --> 00:17:53,797
Do you want to be on the same team as

261
00:17:53,797 --> 00:17:56,251
Michael Jordan, or do you want to play against him every night?

262
00:17:57,252 --> 00:17:58,252
You want to win, right?

263
00:17:58,252 --> 00:18:01,952
You don't want to play against him every day and keep getting beat.

264
00:18:01,952 --> 00:18:02,540
Yeah, sure, you

265
00:18:02,540 --> 00:18:03,520
may win once in a

266
00:18:03,520 --> 00:18:04,892
while, but you're not going to win

267
00:18:04,892 --> 00:18:06,852
the championship because you've got to go through Michael Jordan.

268
00:18:07,152 --> 00:18:11,752
So the quickest way to win a championship is to be on the same team as Michael Jordan.

269
00:18:13,452 --> 00:18:19,352
So, with that in mind, institutional traders, they're always trying to hide what they're doing in the market.

270
00:18:20,252 --> 00:18:23,636
The reason they're doing that is because the size of

271
00:18:23,636 --> 00:18:27,020
their order is often very big, and they use all

272
00:18:27,020 --> 00:18:33,450
different types of order entries to minimize the market impact when they're getting in and out of a position.

273
00:18:35,052 --> 00:18:35,940
You know, they've

274
00:18:35,940 --> 00:18:38,012
got thousands and thousands of lots to

275
00:18:38,012 --> 00:18:42,749
buy. And, you know, you can't just bully your way through the market to fill it.

276
00:18:43,252 --> 00:18:51,852
You want to do it with the least market impact, you know, without moving the price as much as possible.

277
00:18:52,352 --> 00:18:57,052
You know, if you could do it without impacting the price, then that's great. It's more money in their pockets.

278
00:18:58,552 --> 00:19:04,052
But one thing that they can't hide is the fact that they traded. It will show up in the volume.

279
00:19:04,952 --> 00:19:08,552
The volume provides the intensity of a price movement.

280
00:19:08,752 --> 00:19:13,452
If price starts moving, you'll see the volume should really pick up if it's a true move.

281
00:19:13,552 --> 00:19:17,152
You'll see price movements on very thin volume, but then what happens?

282
00:19:17,252 --> 00:19:18,152
The price just...

283
00:19:18,552 --> 00:19:22,552
You know, falls right back after it moves up on thin volume.

284
00:19:22,952 --> 00:19:29,552
But if price is moving on heavy volume, it's indicative of a real strong, solid move.

285
00:19:31,152 --> 00:19:37,552
This right here is a chart of a nice move down, and you're seeing very strong strong selling coming in.

286
00:19:37,552 --> 00:19:43,352
You got the imbalances, you got very nice volume, you got negative deltas all the way down.

287
00:19:43,352 --> 00:19:48,052
You got 1900 sold there, 1200 sold here, 891.

288
00:19:48,852 --> 00:19:56,852
Even here, these are not imbalances, but they're heavy volume. It's 2500, 2400. You can see the volume is quite strong.

289
00:20:01,164 --> 00:20:03,864
Again, this is another example.

290
00:20:04,264 --> 00:20:08,464
The market is starting to move up, and you're seeing it happen on strong buying.

291
00:20:09,764 --> 00:20:13,964
Buying and balance of $1,200, getting volume of $2,100, $2,400.

292
00:20:14,464 --> 00:20:17,564
What's selling? A couple hundred, $800, $1,900.

293
00:20:18,164 --> 00:20:23,764
Here you've got $2,000 against $400, $600 against $2,000.

294
00:20:24,064 --> 00:20:26,364
It's strong buying on the way back up.

295
00:20:31,464 --> 00:20:33,164
This is a different price. This is crude.

296
00:20:33,964 --> 00:20:39,064
And what you're seeing is you're seeing volume up here. It's to stop it, stop the move higher.

297
00:20:39,164 --> 00:20:40,164
It's the same price.

298
00:20:40,164 --> 00:20:43,590
People are trying to take it higher, but there's somebody up here at this

299
00:20:43,590 --> 00:20:47,262
price here that has volume. They don't want the market to get past that level.

300
00:20:48,264 --> 00:20:50,464
They may let it go past by a

301
00:20:50,464 --> 00:20:54,864
tick or two, but there's somebody that has a lot of inventory to sell up here.

302
00:20:55,364 --> 00:21:01,164
And, you know, order flows is, you know, the only way you can determine that.

303
00:21:07,252 --> 00:21:08,652
This is a five-year chart, right?

304
00:21:08,652 --> 00:21:16,752
And you're seeing a nice move up from a low, and you're seeing massive buying, 5,000 imbalances, 5,000, 4,000.

305
00:21:18,252 --> 00:21:25,352
When normally you're seeing imbalances of a few hundred, you're seeing these massive imbalances, 5,000, 5,000, 4,000.

306
00:21:26,052 --> 00:21:30,252
You know, big positive deltas as the market is moving away from the low.

307
00:21:30,852 --> 00:21:31,730
You know, you

308
00:21:31,730 --> 00:21:33,780
see right on the low, you see

309
00:21:33,780 --> 00:21:35,830
a small print as well, indicating that

310
00:21:35,830 --> 00:21:39,051
there's not much interest in people to sell it down here.

311
00:21:39,452 --> 00:21:40,297
You know, in

312
00:21:40,297 --> 00:21:42,269
the move up, you're seeing a single

313
00:21:42,269 --> 00:21:45,649
print. Again, there's not much interest for people to sell it lower.

314
00:21:52,164 --> 00:21:53,764
This is a bond chart.

315
00:21:54,564 --> 00:22:02,764
And what you're seeing here, you're seeing just average ratio numbers, but you're seeing a lot of selling.

316
00:22:03,964 --> 00:22:07,564
On the way up, you've got a couple of imbalances, but it turns right up here.

317
00:22:08,064 --> 00:22:13,164
And what happens in the delta is very strong negative at the end of a move.

318
00:22:13,164 --> 00:22:20,364
You have the market moved up, kind of moved up on some okay volume, okay deltas.

319
00:22:21,964 --> 00:22:24,864
But you hit the high and there's a lot of selling came in.

320
00:22:25,064 --> 00:22:27,164
You see the selling imbalance right off the high.

321
00:22:27,664 --> 00:22:31,164
You have a buying imbalance right here. People were trying to take it to go higher.

322
00:22:31,364 --> 00:22:34,164
Earlier in the bar, people were buying it. You got the buying imbalance.

323
00:22:34,564 --> 00:22:35,764
They couldn't push it any higher.

324
00:22:35,764 --> 00:22:42,964
And it was bid here at 22, 23. And someone just came in and sold the heck out of it.

325
00:22:43,064 --> 00:22:49,464
You got this big buying imbalance, 400, and just sold it off. And the market just sold lower.

326
00:22:50,564 --> 00:22:55,364
I mean, this is why you want to look at an order flow chart.

327
00:22:55,464 --> 00:23:00,864
You could see this happening in real time and get in on the move when it's happening.

328
00:23:01,764 --> 00:23:03,964
Not getting in down here after it's returned.

329
00:23:04,064 --> 00:23:05,590
You can get in as soon as you

330
00:23:05,590 --> 00:23:06,926
notice that it turned, and you can

331
00:23:06,926 --> 00:23:08,262
get a nice profit out of it.

332
00:23:09,864 --> 00:23:15,764
So, you know, that's the end of this lesson, lesson five, market participants.

333
00:23:16,464 --> 00:23:18,532
In the next lesson, I'll explain the different

334
00:23:18,532 --> 00:23:20,600
types of trading being done in the market

335
00:23:20,600 --> 00:23:23,961
by the market participants and how to interpret what the heck they're doing.

336
00:23:24,464 --> 00:23:25,789
I mean, like I said,

337
00:23:25,789 --> 00:23:27,645
there's all sorts of different market participants,

338
00:23:27,645 --> 00:23:29,236
but you want to understand why

339
00:23:29,236 --> 00:23:30,561
they're doing what they're doing.

340
00:23:31,364 --> 00:23:40,964
You know, it's one thing to know, you know, that, you know, that they're buying, you know, who's buying.

341
00:23:40,964 --> 00:23:42,249
But, you know, you want

342
00:23:42,249 --> 00:23:44,049
to take everything into context with what's

343
00:23:44,049 --> 00:23:46,363
going on and know how to profit from it.

344
00:23:47,164 --> 00:23:50,964
So that's the end of Lesson 5, and we'll pick things up in Lesson 6.

